From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nowon <nowon@noreply.pepecoin.surf>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 15:45:22 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 156/162] GreatDANE: prep lazy node mode (namespace sync,
 on-demand zones)

When greatdane.node.lazy is on (default false until Keeper's flag
lands), spawn the embedded node with a placeholder CLI flag and env
name (TODO-KEEPER-FLAG). The TLSA verifier and error trap treat
SERVFAIL+EDE(loading) or /gd/tlsa status "loading" as "zone still
fetching": wait up to greatdane.node.lazyTimeoutSec (default 10),
then show a retryable GD_ZONE_LOADING page. That state is never a
key-pinning or cert rejection. Plain SERVFAIL without the Keeper EDE
(TODO-KEEPER-EDE, still 0/unassigned) stays on the existing
fail-closed path.

Name suggestions are unchanged: they read /gd/names from the
namespace, which lazy sync still keeps complete.

Local test: greatdane/tests/lazy_node (localhost stub, no mach, no
real mesh). Do not push.
